Completes the native StormFlix playback architecture across Web, Android and TV/Fire while preserving Direct Play first and forbidding silent video transcoding.

Implemented:
- capability-aware PlaybackPlan with codec, resolution, frame-rate, HDR and optional bitrate policy;
- exact selected-audio execution through seekable remux/AAC adapters;
- server-side preferred audio selection for browsers that cannot reliably select multi-audio tracks;
- Android/TV MediaCodec capability publication and Media3 PlaybackPlan execution;
- native MediaSession, phone/tablet PiP, and retained D-pad/remote behavior for TV/Fire;
- playback-session continuity across plan/source/version switches;
- browser Media Session position state and PiP controls;
- deterministic regression coverage for video policy, multi-audio, exact execution URLs and sessions;
- updated CHANGELOG.md, PROJECT_STATE.md and PLAYBACK_ARCHITECTURE.md marking the unified playback architecture complete.

Policy remains explicit: no silent video transcoding or tone mapping.

## Objetivo
Criar a fundação técnica do PS_Orchestrator, sem publicar ainda o fluxo completo de onboarding antes de fechar a idempotência do primeiro passo no PS_Empresa.

## Incluído
- Java 25 + Spring Boot 4.1.1;
- Spring Cloud 2025.1.3 + OpenFeign;
- clientes para PS_Empresa, PS_User, PS_Contrato e PS_Login usando os contratos atuais;
- propagação de `X-Internal-Key` e `X-Correlation-Id`;
- proteção de futuras rotas `/internal/**`;
- `/version` e Actuator health;
- Swagger/OpenAPI;
- Docker Java 25;
- CI com Maven verify, JaCoCo 90/70 e Docker build;
- configuração `prod` por variáveis de ambiente.

## Decisão arquitetural
O endpoint completo de onboarding não entra neste PR porque PS_User e PS_Contrato já são idempotentes por `onboardingId`, mas PS_Empresa ainda não possui mecanismo equivalente. Publicar a orquestração antes de resolver isso criaria uma janela de inconsistência em falha parcial.

## Próximo passo
Fechar idempotência/recuperação do primeiro passo de Empresa e então implementar a máquina de orquestração Empresa → MASTER → Contrato → convite Login.

Frontend, Gateway e mensageria permanecem fora de escopo.

## Aanleiding
De eerste `BREBO Zoho missing item diagnosis` stopte met exit code 255 voordat er diagnose-uitvoer verscheen.

## Oorzaak
De workflow draaide losse `php -r` code met `auto_prepend_file`. De bewezen migratieworkflow draait dezelfde runtime-initialisatie via Drush. Daardoor was deze diagnose afwijkend van de werkende productie-uitvoeringsroute.

## Fix
- voer de diagnose uit via dezelfde Drush-runtime als de werkende Zoho-migratie;
- controleer expliciet of de runtime-credentials geladen zijn;
- houd IMAP read-only;
- log nog steeds uitsluitend UID en metadata-aanwezigheid/body byte-lengte, geen onderwerp/adressen/mailinhoud.

Geen wijziging aan migratiecursor, Communications of mailboxen.

## ETW-A0 — PREPARED / PROMOTION BLOCKED

This stacked PR is the dedicated A0 execution branch. It starts from the validated eTwin programme head `1c62ae02faf7c88e4743e0b089ac2f76cb819bf2` and consumes CEW contract baseline `cab1c53b62b2b70294b6b7e8d7dddd14ccdcb832` for preparation only.

### Implemented

- frozen CEW contract fingerprint: lifecycle P0-P16, development model, GOV.UK human-centred model, usability metrics and source registry;
- `Project`, `Discipline`, `ProjectDisciplineScope`, `ScopeContext` contract;
- initial scopes:
  - `N12 / STRUCTURES = ACTIVE + CEW_BOUND`;
  - `N12 / ARCHITECTURE = NOT_YET_RELEASED` with read-only source inventory only;
  - `TEST_PROJECT / STRUCTURES = TEST_ONLY` with zero N12 engineering data;
- read-only `CEWSourceInventoryAdapter`;
- architectural source count derived from the frozen registry (`classe=architettonica`), not hard-coded;
- fail-closed scope runtime for route/query/cache/async/deep-link/history primitives;
- independent Security Isolation and Authority Audit prep receipts;
- CEW/GOV.UK-derived A0 usability/HVA task set;
- integrated A0 preparation validator and CI;
- orchestrator owner result `PREP_PASS` and deterministic ingest rehearsal.

### Observed preparation result

Validated same-head cycle on `f97729e1c800ed14314ee0d8b2436df2af987ae2`:

- Validate eTwin Platform Identity Boundary — PASS (`33151178271`)
- Validate eTwin Program Orchestration — PASS (`33151178257`)
- Validate N12 Knowledge System — PASS (`33151178260`)

Observed invariants:

- Architecture source inventory = 4 source documents derived from CEW registry;
- Architecture domain entities = 0;
- Architecture domain properties = 0;
- TEST_PROJECT source count = 0;
- cross-project leakage = false;
- cross-discipline leakage = false;
- no persisted project/source binding introduced in A0;
- no ArchitecturalEntity / CrossDisciplineRelation introduced;
- no SourceVersion or N12 engineering mutation.

### Orchestrated state

`ETW-A0 = PREPARED_BLOCKED_PROMOTION`

`preparation_decision = PREP_PASS`

`ETW-A1 = WAITING`

The CI rehearses `PREP_ONLY -> PREP_PASS -> PREPARED_BLOCKED_PROMOTION` through `scripts/etw_orchestrator.py` and then restores/validates the persisted blocked queue state.

### Promotion blockers

A0 is **not COMPLETE** and this PR is intentionally draft. Promotion requires all of:

- `CEW_PROMOTED_BASELINE`;
- Human Factors/HVA execution;
- Production smoke;
- `APPROVE_PLATFORM_BOUNDARY`.

Until those are satisfied, the orchestrator returns `BLOCKED_DEPENDENCY` with no selected work item and must not release ETW-A1.

### Durable receipts

- `automation/receipts/etw-platform/ETW-A0-SECURITY-ISOLATION-PREP.json`
- `automation/receipts/etw-platform/ETW-A0-AUTHORITY-AUDIT-PREP.json`
- `automation/receipts/etw-platform/ETW-A0-PREP-PASS_v1.json`

### Authority boundary

This PR prepares only the eTwin platform identity/context layer. CEW remains the Structures/Existing Structures authority; N12 engineering authority is unchanged. Source availability does not create Architecture domain truth, and no human engineering authority is exercised here.

## What changed

- bump the Data Foundation browser cache key so stale pre-fix coverage snapshots are not reused;
- present S&P 500 membership as the universe dimension rather than a peer category to exchange listing;
- relabel the exchange counts as `NYSE-listed` and `Nasdaq-listed` and put the S&P 500 universe count first.

Expected presentation: `499 S&P 500 universe · 342 NYSE-listed · 157 Nasdaq-listed` when the live corpus is fully indexed.

No backend, retrieval, research, or ingestion semantics change.

