Moves the UI modernization from Hop's outer shell into shared dialog/form infrastructure without rewriting individual plugins or replacing native SWT controls.

## Changes

- add semantic `DIALOG_MARGIN`, `DIALOG_ELEMENT_GAP` and `FORM_LABEL_GAP` tokens to `HopUiTheme`;
- route `BaseDialog`'s shared spacing constants through the theme;
- align `LabelText`, `LabelTextVar`, `LabelCombo` and `LabelComboVar` on one label-to-control gap;
- make `LabelText` explicitly inherit Hop look/background handling like the other shared form composites;
- add a generic `scripts/apply-ui-patch.sh` entry point while keeping `apply-phase1.sh` intentionally scoped through 1C;
- generalize the patch manager/state model through Phase 2;
- migrate existing state-v1 Phase 1 checkouts only after verifying their recorded hashes/phase markers;
- document the Phase 2/3 plan and updated workflow.

## Non-goals

- no per-transform/action dialog rewrites;
- no owner-drawn text/combo/button controls;
- no font replacement;
- no changes to field semantics, validation, tab order or plugin business logic.

## Validation

Actions run 33176601303 is green. CI verifies:

1. clean application through Phase 2;
2. repeated application is a byte-for-byte no-op in the generated Hop diff;
3. a complete Phase 1 checkout is detected with Phase 2 missing and upgrades to the same final diff;
4. legacy patch-manager state version 1 migrates safely and converges to the same final diff;
5. unrelated local changes remain rejected;
6. the patched Apache Hop 2.19.0 sources pass `./mvnw -pl ui,engine -am -DskipTests package` on Java 21.

Phase 3 will be kept separate and will focus on the shared `TableView`/preview-grid surface.

